; `US$` is not a currency, so this posting line matches no rule. It used to be
; skipped — along with every posting after it in the same transaction —
; leaving a transaction with fewer legs, a silently wrong balance, and nothing
; in the output to say so. `bean_core`'s loader carried a tripwire
; (`dropped_posting_warning`) precisely because of it.
;
; It is a syntax error now. A ledger that cannot be read is better than a
; ledger that reads wrong.
2026-01-15 * "the second leg is unparseable"
  Expenses:Groceries  42.50 USD
  Assets:Bank:Checking  -42.50 US$
  Assets:Cash  0 USD
